 "notes": "Headline ALP-photon result from Fig.3: 95% C.L. exclusion region in the (m_a, g_agamma) plane from a joint fit to Tibet ASgamma + HAWC + HEGRA + MAGIC Crab Nebula gamma-ray spectra (chi^2<53.4). Coupling already in canonical L=-(1/4)g a F Ftilde convention (paper Eq.1, g_agamma=1/f). Excluded region consists of TWO disjoint closed lobes, both open at the top (g>1e-9, off-plot); points are the vector outlines of both lobes in native traversal order (path9 left lobe first, then path10 right lobe), NOT monotonic in mass. Deepest exclusion g~1.3e-10 GeV^-1 at m~4e-7 eV (abstract quotes 'below 1.8e-10 for 2-6e-7 eV'). Axes log-log; calibration cross-checked against the overplotted CAST 6.6e-11 GeV^-1 horizontal line. Limit is from photon-ALP oscillation in the galactic B-field, independent of DM density. This paper also sets a dark-photon kinetic-mixing limit (Fig.4, eps>1e-3, DarkPhoton) but the ALP g_agamma bound is the headline result.",
